  "content": "[Intro]\n[Dadd9]\n[C]\n[Dadd9]\n[C]\n\n[Verse 1]\n[Dadd9]Wrapped up in some powdered wool I\n[C]guess I'm loosing touch. Don't\n[Dadd9]tell me this is dying, 'cos\n[C]I ain't changed that much. The\n[F/G]only sound is water drops, I\n[G/F]wonder where the hell I am,\n[A]Some kind of jam? [A7/G]Coc-\n[F#m]koo Cocoon [G#m]have I come [F#m]to, too [G#m]soon for\n[F#/B]you? There's\n\n[Verse 2]\n[Dadd9]nothing I can recognize; This is\n[C]nowhere that I've known. With\n[Dadd9]no sign of life at all, I\n[C]guess that I'm alone. And\n[F/G]feel so secure That I\n[G/F]know this can't be real\n[A]But I feel [A7/G]good. Coc-\n[F#m]koo Cocoon [G#m]have I come [F#m]to, too [G#m]soon for\n[F#/B]you?\n\n[Intrelude]\n[G/A]\n[F/G]\n[D/C]\n[Bb]\n[Dm]  [Bb]\n[C]\n[Dadd9]\n[C]I\n\n[Verse 3]\n[Dadd9]wonder if I'm prisoner Locked\n[C]up in some Brooklyn jail Or\n[Dadd9]some sort of Jonah Shut\n[C]up inside the whale. No,\n[F/G]I'm still Rael And I'm\n[G/F]stuck in some kind of cave.\n[A]What could have saved [A7/G]me? Coc-\n[F#m]koo Cocoon [G#m]have I come [F#m]to, too [G#m]soon for\n[F#/B]you?\n\n[Outro]\n[G/A]\n[F/G]\n[D/C]\n[Bb]\n[Dm]  [Bb]\n[C]\n[D/F#]",
